    {
      "id": 24,
      "title": "The client (browser) \u2014 what the user actually experienced",
      "type": "row",
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": [],
      "description": "Counts, never rates: failures and calls over 1s always ship, ordinary successes are sampled at 10%. So these totals are absolute, but dividing them by the call count would overstate the error rate roughly tenfold. A true error rate comes from the gateway.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 31
